  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the scene as the speaker of the racially charged statement",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the scene where the man in the foreground is depicted as the speaker of the hateful statement. The text 'see... i told you cyril.' implies that the user is identifying with or imagining themselves as the person making the accusation, projecting their own viewpoint or attitude onto the visual and textual elements of the meme. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictics like 'you' or 'me' in the text, but the framing of the meme as a direct address ('see... i told you') creates an implicit projection of the user as the one who is 'telling' or 'showing' the statement to Cyril Ramaphosa, thereby positioning the user as the speaker or the one who holds the viewpoint being expressed. This projection is onto the scene, which includes both the visual material (the laughing man) and the textual material (the hateful statement), making the scene the primary entity onto which the user is projected.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
